            "count": 2,
            "creation_time": "2019-03-28T16:06:34Z"
          },
          {
            "count": 3,
            "is_markdown": false,
            "bug_id": 16135,
            "text": "(In reply to Martin Maechler from comment #2)\n> (In reply to Benjamin Tyner from comment #1)\n> > Created attachment 2412 [details]\n> > patch for stats::convolve\n> \n> Didn't have time yet to look... but I have had my own patch for years...\n> which instead of changing the behavior of one type also introduces new\n> 'type's  allowing some back compatibility...\n> \n> Ben, maybe we can look at both... or I also post my patch (several files,\n> notably also documentation) here...\n\nMartin, I'd be interested to see the details of what you're thinking here. To me, the current behavior seems unintuitive:\n\n> convolve( 1:5, rep(1, 5), type='filter')\n[1] 15\n> convolve( 1:5, rep(1, 4), type='filter')\n[1] 10 14\n> convolve( 1:5, rep(1, 3), type='filter')\n[1]  6  9 12\n> convolve( 1:5, rep(1, 2), type='filter')\n[1] 3 5 7 9\n> convolve( 1:5, rep(1, 1), type='filter')\n[1] 2 3 4\n\nas it is hard (for me) to imagine this was the intended outcome.",
            "creation_time": "2019-04-02T02:54:19Z",
