            "id": 102637,
            "creation_time": "2026-02-20T17:53:51Z",
            "count": 4,
            "text": "Created attachment 3611\nUpdated convolve patch with ?convolve improvements and tests\n\nA few observations:\n\n`?convolve` has [1]\n\n> numeric sequences _of the same length_ to be convolved.\n\nBut AIUI that is only required for `type=\"circular\"`, e.g. as written just below [2]:\n\n> If `type == \"circular\"`, [`length(x) = length(y)`] is required\n\nNext, I'm no FFT expert, and I don't have access right now to the Brillinger text linked at the end, but the wording here [3] isn't precise enough for me:\n\n> For `\"open\"` and `\"filter\"`, the sequences are padded with `0`s (from left and right) first; `\"filter\"` returns the middle sub-vector of `\"open\"`, namely, the result of running a weighted mean of `x` with weights `y`.\n\nI think \"middle sub-vector\" in particular is not easily intuited.\n\nThe examples Benjamin provides with `y = rep(1, N)` imply the \"middle sub-vector\" is perhaps more easily understood as \"the sub-vector not requiring 0-padding\" or \"the vector after filtering out those built from 0-padding\" or precisely `k = m, ..., n` when `m<=n` (using the index `k` from the formula [4]).\n\nThat would then imply that the wording \"namely, the result of running a weighted mean of `x` with weights `y`\" is _only for the `length(x)=length(y)` case_.\n\nWith that preamble in mind, I am inclined to agree with Ben that this example is a plain bug -- the result should have length 5, not 3.\n\nThat said, I don't find Ben's patch satisfactory, since it will run into a similar edge case problem when `length(y) > length(x)`, in which case we should return `numeric(0)`, because we always rely on 0-padding, as the current code achieves:\n\n```\n# under proposed patch\nconvolve(1:5, rep(1,6), type='filter')\n# [1] 15 15\n\n# in r-devel\nconvolve(1:5, rep(1,6), type='filter')\n# numeric(0)\n```\n\nI'm attaching a different patch to solve both problems, as well as taking a stab at improving the documentation.\n\nTracked at https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/235\n\n[1] https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/blob/5891760c29285562cfb0d1c5513625a93150e2a0/src/library/stats/man/convolve.Rd#L17-L18\n[2] https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/blob/5891760c29285562cfb0d1c5513625a93150e2a0/src/library/stats/man/convolve.Rd#L46\n[3] https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/blob/5891760c29285562cfb0d1c5513625a93150e2a0/src/library/stats/man/convolve.Rd#L25-L28\n[4] https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/blob/5891760c29285562cfb0d1c5513625a93150e2a0/src/library/stats/man/convolve.Rd#L42-L44",
            "bug_id": 16135,
